{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1021207-rage-across-the-holiday-sale-need-advice-on-what-to-buy","id":1021207,"title":"Rage Across the Holiday Sale - Need advice on what to buy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-23T03:14:42-08:00","id":1021207,"title":"Rage Across the Holiday Sale - Need advice on what to buy","content":"It's the year's best season and Werewolf tittles are on sale, so I need some advice on what to buy.<br /> <br /> I already own W20, but none of the W20 sourcebooks, and none of the Revised or Second Edition sourcebooks. Thus, I have the following questions:<br /> <br /> - Does W20 Book of the Wyrm cover all the content from Book of the Wyrm second edition?<br /> <br /> - How about W20 Umbra, does it cover all the content from Umbra (Revised)?<br /> <br /> - What Second or Revised Edition books I need to cover all the lore relevant to spirits and the spiritual world/cosmology, besides Wyrm and Umbra?<br /> <br /> - Do I need to buy Possessed and Freak Legion, if I want to cover these kinds of antagonists, or are W20 sourcebooks enough?<br /> <br /> - I'm really into evil, utter deranged, stuff (as a Storyteller, of course), so what products could be labelled as &quot;Black Dog&quot; sourcebooks?<br /> <br /> Thanks for your attention and Merry Christmas/Holidays/Yule!<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T05:26:13-08:00","id":1021236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1021207-rage-across-the-holiday-sale-need-advice-on-what-to-buy#post1021207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> - Do I need to buy Possessed and Freak Legion, if I want to cover these kinds of antagonists, or are W20 sourcebooks enough?<br /> <br /> - I'm really into evil, utter deranged, stuff (as a Storyteller, of course), so what products could be labelled as &quot;Black Dog&quot; sourcebooks?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't necessarily need to buy them, but they're both filled with great information that can add more to your games. Freak Legion is one of my favorite books ever produced by White Wolf. Ever. So I think you'll find plenty of use for it. Possessed is good, too. Though it definitely feels a bit lighter than Freak Legion when it comes to the horror and disturbing content(which I love).<br /> <br /> They don't make them like that anymore IMO, unfortunately. <br /> <br /> Another book that's great for antagonists is Subsidiaries of Pentex, which gives you a lot more insight into the inner-workings of various Pentex businesses like Avalon, Tellus, and King Distilleries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T09:34:07-08:00","id":1021302,"title":"","content":"I went ahead and got, hammer and klaive, and Chronicles of the black labyrinth<br /> <br /> Allready had a print copy of the latter, but cant find it anymore, and its convenient to look through it at length on my e Reader.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T19:56:19-08:00","id":1021462,"title":"","content":"I'd highly recommend a book on the Umbra as it's an important aspect of the setting and Garou culture that is often overlooked and underrepresented in games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T08:12:49-08:00","id":1021575,"title":"","content":"The W20 books choose different places to emphasize over their non-20 counterparts, but I would HIGHLY recommend the Book of the Wyrm 20. It is fascinating and brings the baddies firmly into modern times. I loved it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2197-roleplayrose","name":"roleplayrose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2197_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}